{
  "description": "Unified Flutter coding rules for Plattr Pro.",
  "file_patterns": ["lib/**/*.dart", "lib/router.dart", "lib/pages/app_routes.dart"],
  "guidelines": [
    "[Architecture] Respect the existing clean architecture, Flutter 3.x, and Material 3 design conventions; introduce new structures only when the current patterns cannot be extended.",
    "[Architecture] Model domain data with Freezed, keep *_state.dart classes on ChangeNotifier, and place API calls in dedicated *_repository.dart files returning ApiResponse wrappers.",
    "[State] Manage loading and error states explicitly, notify listeners only when data actually changes, dispose resources in dispose(), and keep each provider focused on a single feature with minimal coupling.",
    "[State] Inject repositories/services through the established dependency mechanism, document significant state transitions, and keep global utilities (logger, API constants) under singletonGods/.",
    "[UI] Build small, focused widgets that use const constructors, meaningful keys, clean layouts, and shallow hierarchies while honoring platform-specific design nuances.",
    "[Performance] Minimize rebuilds with const widgets, memoization, and targeted ValueNotifiers; optimize scrolling with ListView.builder/pagination and aggressive image caching.",
    "[Performance] Release resources promptly, reduce redundant computations, avoid heavy platform channel calls unless essential, and leverage tree shaking or deferred loading for large features.",
    "[Routing] Declare new routes in app_routes.dart first, keep GoRouter the single source of truth in router.dart, and follow the '/feature-name' naming convention for paths.",
    "[Widgets] Optimize widget lifecycle hooks, prefer composition over deep nesting, and ensure UI code consumes state via Consumer/Selector for precise rebuild control.",
    "[Quality] Implement robust error handling across layers, reuse existing solutions before adding new ones, and align code with the broader project organization to keep the codebase consistent."
  ]
}
